# Rust hot path

Rust owns: crypto, state roots, RocksDB, EVM kernels. Python orchestrates; do not move orchestration into `abs_native` without an ADR.

- Fail-closed errors: `thiserror` / `anyhow`. No unjustified `.unwrap()` / `.expect()`.
- Keep lock sections short. Avoid clone-as-default on hot loops.
- Structured `tracing` spans on I/O and consensus-adjacent paths.
- PyO3 marshalling: tight boundaries; do not hold the GIL across blocking RocksDB/EVM work.
- Cargo features (e.g. `libp2p`) stay opt-in; default wheel stays lean.

```rust
// ❌ BAD
let root = compute_state_root(batch).unwrap();

// ✅ GOOD
let root = compute_state_root(batch)
    .context("state root for batch")?;
```

When behavior changes, extend native tests **and** the industrial/mesh gate — pytest-only is not acceptance.
